118 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (I'm sure many of us have made trips to the supermarket and seen a wide variety of organic foods. Many of us associate organic foods with being healthier and more expensive, but why is that so? This article will explore why organic foods are much more expensive than regular foods.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
119 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The definition of organic refers to the system of farming and food production; it is produced without the use of pesticides and other artificial chemicals that can be found in fertilizers. This means that in order to classify produce or farming methods as organic, we need to ensure that no artificial chemicals are used. )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
120 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (First and foremost, organic foods are chemical-free. Organic farms do not use chemicals, synthetic pesticides and GMOs \(Genetically Modified Organisms\) to help with farming, but why do non-organic farms use non-natural methods? This is because non-organic methods of farming reduce the amount of labour needed and are more cost-effective. Therefore sparing them the need to hire more workers to carry out manual labour such as hand-weeding, cleaning up polluted water and more. Resulting in organic farming spending more money, time and effort, which is reflected dearly in their hefty prices. People will have to pay more for all the hard work that goes into growing organic foods.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
121 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Secondly, high demand cannot match the low supply. It is no secret that organic foods are highly sought after. This is likely due to the widespread belief that organic foods are healthier than conventional food. Studies have shown that organic foods have a moderate increase in nutrients as well as a decrease in cadmium levels compared to non-organic foods.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
122 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (What is Cadmium? Cadmium is a toxic metal found in soils which are absorbed by plants. While fewer dangerous bacteria are found in organic meat, non-organic foods are still within health guidelines and are equally edible. Despite proof that non-organic foods are safe, people still prefer organic foods. Due to these reasons, there is a high demand for organic foods. As a longer time is required for organic foods to grow and the high demand for them, the prices rose. )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
123 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (In addition, the process of growing organic food is tedious, and the cost of producing it is expensive. More labour is required as many procedures have to be followed. For example, because organic food has a higher class level, it needs to be both safe for consumption while being healthy at the same time. Organic foods are to be kept untouched to keep up to these standards, only allowing organic foods to be in contact with water. Due to all this tedious work that organic farmers have to deal with, they are often rewarded with more commission when they sell their organic foods. )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
124 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText <>
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
