177 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (In many games, this creates a situation where players who do not spend money \(Free- to- Play players\) are severely disadvantaged, making it exceedingly troublesome for them to compete or progress in a specific game.  In stark contrast, the players who spend money on the game \(Pay-to-Win players\) become gods among men, giving players a power trip as they rampage through other weaker players. Exempli gratia, the multiplayer online action role-playing video game Diablo Immortal. When a player hits higher levels, the difficulty for progression for free-to-play players increases exponentially as a result of massive experience point reductions coupled with terrible drop rates. The only thing free-to-play players can turn to for further progression is to convert to a pay-to-win player and use in-game currency to buy loot boxes coined 'legendary crests' in Diablo Immortal for a slim chance of obtaining something good. More often than not, players will be throwing their money away. Therefore, the use of pay-to-win mechanics is another tactic of predatory monetisation.)
/E (In many games, this creates a situation where players who do not spend money \(Free- to- Play players\) are severely disadvantaged, making it exceedingly troublesome for them to compete or progress in a specific game.  In stark contrast, the players who spend money on the game \(Pay-to-Win players\) become gods among men, giving players a power trip as they rampage through other weaker players. Exempli gratia, the multiplayer online action role-playing video game Diablo Immortal. When a player hits higher levels, the difficulty for progression for free-to-play players increases exponentially as a result of massive experience point reductions coupled with terrible drop rates. The only thing free-to-play players can turn to for further progression is to convert to a pay-to-win player and use in-game currency to buy loot boxes coined 'legendary crests' in Diablo Immortal for a slim chance of obtaining something good. More often than not, players will be throwing their money away. Therefore, the use of pay-to-win mechanics is another tactic of predatory monetisation.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
