/T (To sum up, while in-game purchases can be a legitimate way for game developers to make money, there is a growing concern about the detrimental impacts of predatory monetisation practices and tactics on vulnerable players. Those are children who may not fully understand the consequences of spending money, those with internet gaming disorders or addictions and those who gamble compulsively. I think that the gaming industry needs to have the moral ethics and responsibility to ensure that their games are not exploiting players for profits or exacerbating destructive spending habits. One should also be smart and keep a lookout for these common pitfalls.)
