196 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Furthermore, confession pages punctuate the growth of our schools with Unitians who lead themselves and serve others. It goes against Unity's aim for respect, tainting the school image. Seeing your name in a post with "XXXX looks so good!" may feel good. However, imagine if you were in the shoes of someone who saw their name on a post saying something along the lines of "XXXX has a very bad personality". Such posts develop a toxic environment. By proven results, it has been concluded that cyberbullying can affect someone emotionally, with anxiety, depression, and stress, sometimes for an extended period of time. Many students may share a desire to break the rules sometimes, with the influence of others, but let's not make it a bad habit.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
197 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (From afar, these might seem like rudimentary and unnecessary rules, but even the smallest of things also contribute a factor in how good a school's discipline is. From a positive perspective, these rules were established for everyone's good, to build a good school reputation with future-ready Unitians. Keeping this in mind, let's do our best to follow school rules. Zig Ziglar, an American author who encouraged others to look at the bright side of life, said, "When you do the right things in the right way you have nothing to lose because you have nothing to fear". Following the rules can start with one person and continue with everyone.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
