/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Though it may seem like an unconscious habit, it was exhausting when it first came about. Teachers had to plan their online lessons, be it on Zoom or Student Learning Space \(SLS\), beforehand. They also had to ensure everyone was on task from their homes. For students like us, it had its pros and cons.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
205 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Firstly, we could save a lot of time and money. As it is now once every two weeks, we would not need to wake up extra early to prepare and get ready for school, as we can do our school work on our bed, in our home clothes. Furthermore, we are not limited to food within the canteen and would not need to spend any money on food, so we would not have to worry about that. Therefore, it is very convenient to do schoolwork at home.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
206 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Additionally, we can complete our homework at our own time and own pace. This helped me understand my concepts better. I could slowly learn without the pressure of finishing the work in the given period of the lessons. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
207 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (We learnt to be more self-directed and responsible for our learning as the work would usually be due by the end of the day, so we could manage our time properly to get everything done. Therefore, studying at home is very beneficial for students.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
208 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText <>
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
209 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Moreover, as homes are usually shared spaces between family members, having personal space with all their needs is challenging, from good wifi connections to a well-lit study area for the whole day. In particular, those who share a room with a family member are most affected as they would need to share everything and may also unknowingly bother each other. Some may feel uncomfortable when their family members are there when studying. This affects their studies as they do not feel comfortable enough to do their work at home without their family members disturbing them. Therefore, students may study poorly at home because of the lack of personal space.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
210 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (All in all, getting used to working and studying at home was a new and complicated experience, with all the ups and downs, and one we can all learn from. Adapting quickly to get back on track was quite tricky. The pandemic has made us realize how much we take things for granted, so we should all persevere and look at the positive side of things, looking forward to the near future when the new standard can be called normal.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
