214 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (We all have worries, don't we? Whether it's about our studies, our futures, or more, they tend to trap us in a loop of apprehension every time we think about it. This feeling is no different from the concerns your friends may be facing around today's environmental issues. Statistics and social media posts often paint a grim picture of the climate situation we live in. "The Climate Disaster Is Here", "Code Red For Humanity", and "Warning On Escalating Climate Crisis", just to name a few. When these terrifying headlines are paired with pictures of flaming forest fires or people struggling to escape a heavy flood, wouldn't you be concerned too?)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
215 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Even in the coldest regions of our planet, global warming overpowers them all. A study by the journal, Science, has found that nearly half of the world's glaciers outside of the Greenland and Antarctic ice sheets will melt by the end of the century, even if the world's ambitious global warming goal is met. As a result, we will be suffering the consequences of the Earth's rising sea levels much earlier than we may have realised. The mean sea level around Singapore is projected to rise by up to 1 metre by 2100. With one-third of our country being less than five metres above sea level, we are especially vulnerable to large-scale flooding and erosion of our garden city.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
